// Known product issues currently reproduced by integration tests.
//
// Key: "<test file relative to repo root>::<jest fullName>" — fullName is all
// describe titles plus the test title, joined with single spaces. A key
// without the "::<name>" part covers every failure in the file, including
// suite-level load errors. A key naming a describe block covers every test
// nested under it.
//
// The failures-only reporter flags matching failures as KNOWN ISSUE locally
// and in CI job logs, and bakes the ticket into .jest-run-summary.jsonl so
// Barmin can split Slack reports into known vs UNTRACKED failures. When a
// listed test passes, the reporter nudges you to remove the entry.
//
// Optional "envs" scopes an entry to the environments where the bug
// reproduces: "dev", "bugt", "prod", "local". Omit it when the bug is
// environment-independent. A scoped entry is KNOWN only on the listed
// environments; failing elsewhere reports as UNTRACKED with a pointer back
// to the ticket (a tracked bug reaching a new environment is an event —
// comment on the ticket and widen the list). Unmapped registries resolve to
// "local" and match every entry, so local-platform runs are unaffected. The
// "passed" nudge only fires on listed environments, and Barmin promotes an
// entry to a removal candidate only when it was green on all of them in the
// same run.
//
// Full-line comments only — no trailing comments. File tickets with the
// linear-ticket skill; wire entries with the file-known-issue skill. Never
// use test.failing for a product bug: it hides the failure and turns red
// the moment the bug is fixed.
